// =============================================================================
// bonds-course — "Bonds: Lending to Companies and to Countries"
// =============================================================================
// Course TWO of the Stock Market department (Darrell 2026-09-19: "Stock Market
// courses to explore and explain the world of stock and bonds and countries
// that trade and how investment works world wide"). Course one answered STOCK.
// This one answers BONDS, and it is the other half of a single question that
// course one set up and deliberately did not close: a shareholder is paid LAST
// and is owed nothing. A bondholder is paid FIRST and is owed a specific sum on
// a specific date. Everything else about the two instruments follows from that
// one difference in position.
//
// THE ARC, one argument in eight moves:
//   1. A bond is a loan with a receipt        (Psalms 37:21)
//   2. The promise is fixed, so the PRICE moves (Ecclesiastes 5:4, 5)
//   3. Credit: can they actually pay?         (Proverbs 22:7)
//   4. How a COUNTRY borrows                  (Deuteronomy 28:12, 44)
//   5. When a country cannot pay              (2 Kings 4:1, 7)
//   6. The yield curve is a sentence about the future (Proverbs 27:12)
//   7. Inflation: the quiet default           (Isaiah 1:22)
//   8. Usury, the brother, and the stranger   (Deuteronomy 23:19, 20)
//
// WHY LESSON 2 CANNOT BE SKIPPED. "If I am promised a fixed payment, why does
// the price change?" is the question that separates people who understand bonds
// from people who own them. The answer is a single mechanism -- the promise
// cannot move, so the PRICE is the only thing left that can -- and once a reader
// has it, rates, duration and the whole of lesson 6 fall out of it.
//
// THE LINE THIS COURSE HOLDS ON USURY, and it is the hardest one in the
// department (DR-0098). Deuteronomy 23:19-20 is routinely quoted as half a
// verse. The whole of it forbids usury to a BROTHER and permits it to a
// STRANGER, in consecutive clauses, and a house that teaches only the first
// clause is doing the thing this house exists to stop. Lesson 8 teaches BOTH
// clauses from the text, states what they do and do not settle, and refuses
// both over-reaches -- inflating a prohibition aimed at a poor brother into a
// general theory of finance, and explaining it away because it is inconvenient.
// The Banking course holds the same line on Exodus 22:25 and this course does
// not repeat its passages.
//
// AND THE HARD HALF OF LESSON 5. A sovereign default is taught through a
// household (2 Kings 4:1), because the creditor coming for the widow's two sons
// is what a debt crisis is at the bottom of it, and a course that teaches only
// the restructuring arithmetic has taught the least important half. DR-0100:
// the documented harm is stated plainly and it is not inflated either.
//
// VERIFICATION (DR-0076 / SCRIPTURE-REFERENCE-STANDARD). Every quoted span is
// fetched VERBATIM from the repository's own KJV. Our prose says Yahweh;
// quotations keep "God" and "the LORD" exactly as the KJV has them (DR-0210).
// No live figure is quoted anywhere, for the reason course one gives: a number
// printed in a lesson is wrong by the time it is read.
//
// TEACHING, NOT FINANCIAL ADVICE -- carried on the meta.
// =============================================================================

